1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,088
My living room furniture never touches the floor, floating gently near the ceiling in our perfect high-altitude luxury apartment.

2
00:00:08,388 --> 00:00:15,876
Gravity is just a suggestion when you pay enough credits to turn off the pull of the decaying planet below.

3
00:00:16,176 --> 00:00:26,568
Every table, lamp, and chair drifts upward, defying the natural order because my bank account stays permanently full and heavy.

4
00:00:26,868 --> 00:00:36,108
Then the glass floor beneath my expensive floating sofa suddenly cracks with a sharp, terrifying sound that echoes loudly.

5
00:00:36,408 --> 00:00:44,160
I look straight down through the fracture and see hundreds of desperate faces pressed against the underside of my floor.

6
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:52,308
They aren't falling. They are standing flat on the ceiling of their cramped lower level, holding up my entire life.

7
00:00:52,608 --> 00:01:00,168
My floating luxury isn't advanced technology at all. It is just the physical weight of people I forced downward.

8
00:01:00,468 --> 00:01:10,668
The sofa drops heavily, smashing against the floorboards as the illusion of our weightless freedom instantly shatters into dust.

9
00:01:10,968 --> 00:01:17,880
Now my feet touch the cold ground for the very first time, and the pressure of their suffering crushes my chest.

10
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:26,196
If luxury rises because others sink, how heavy is the air you are breathing right now in this exact room?
